# Oracle PL/SQL package calls

- Prefer named notation: `P_PARAM => :bind`.
- For `RAW(16)` GUIDs: use `HEXTORAW('32HEX')` in SQL or bind `Buffer` from Node; in PL/SQL use `SYS_GUID()` or `HEXTORAW`.
- OUT parameters: declare local variables, pass to procedure, then `DBMS_OUTPUT` or return to caller.
- Always use `EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS` in runnable scripts; log `SQLERRM` and `DBMS_UTILITY.FORMAT_ERROR_BACKTRACE`.
- `SYS_REFCURSOR`: open in package/procedure, fetch in loop, `CLOSE` in `FINALLY`-style block or after loop.

## Sample package surface (reference)

Assume `PKG_SAMPLE` with table columns: `ID`, `GUID`, `CODE`, `NAME`, `DESCRIPTION`, `ENTERPRISE_ID`, `ACTIVE_FLAG`, audit columns.

Use realistic names: `p_id`, `p_guid`, `p_code`, `p_name`, `p_description`, `p_enterprise_id`, `p_active_flag`, `p_created_by`, `p_last_updated_by`.
